		(uuid "4233bf8a-34fb-5f6e-ac71-91cb2528b12f")
	)
	(text "Each box is one schematic sheet. A pin name is the net name: pins with the same label are joined.\nSupply rails are not drawn here. They reach every sheet through power symbols:\n  GND      circuit ground. One transformer leg (AC_N behind F1), USB ground and sensor ground.\n  VIN_DC   rectified 24 VAC, 26 to 31 V, 44 V at 32 VAC with no load\n  V_BUCK   5.28 V from the LM5164, present only with 24 VAC. Also feeds the relay coil and the sensor supply.\n  V5       V_BUCK or VBUS through a Schottky diode each: about 4.95 V from 24 VAC, 4.1 to 4.9 V from USB\n  3V3      logic rail, 3.20 to 3.40 V\n  V_DRV    3V3 behind Q3: the opto LED supply, on only while the fail-safe circuit allows drive\n  VBUS     USB-C VBUS\n\nThe nine output channels Z1 to Z8 and MV are nine instances of one sheet, channel.kicad_sch.\nReferences there are 101 to 111 style: the first digit is the channel (9 = master valve), so R301 is\nthe opto LED resistor of zone 3 and Q901 the master valve triac.\n\nBUILD VARIANTS. The base design is the 8-zone build. KiCad variant \"4-zone\" does not fit\ninstances Z5 to Z8 (44 parts), J3 and R28. C52 and C53 are footprints only on both builds.\n\nHOW A VALVE TURNS ON. Firmware toggles KA. Detector A (Failsafe sheet) raises DRV_EN, which releases\nthe expander from reset and switches V_DRV on. Detector B (Expander sheet) turns on Q2. Firmware then\nsets RLY_ON (relay K1 feeds COM) and pulls a ZD_x_N pin low: the opto LED of that channel conducts and\nits triac fires from its own T2. Valve current returns through ISNS and the shunt on the CurrentSense\nsheet. When KA stops, both detectors let go within about a second, each on its own.\n\nConnectivity is taken from hardware/netlist.yaml. The build fails unless the netlist KiCad extracts\nfrom these sheets equals it pin for pin. This design has never been built."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
